@* Reusable navigation for the embedded Keyward sections. Identity-aware (only shown when signed in) and
   localized; uses the KeywardRoutes constants so a host never hardcodes Keyward's route strings. Links are
   grouped by purpose (vaults for people / software credentials for machines) with small section labels; the
   host decides WHERE to place it (its own layout).
   The Groups page (KeywardRoutes.Groups) is deliberately NOT listed here — it is management, so the host
   places it in its administration section (see the reference shell's NavMenu).

   HOST CONTRACT — this component is the one deliberate exception to "every component styles itself": navigation
   belongs to the host's shell, so it renders in the host's navigation vocabulary and ships NO styling of its own.
   The host must style these class names (globally, or with ::deep from its nav container):
     · .nav-group-label — the small section heading above each group (a <div>);
     · .nav-link        — each entry (Blazor's NavLink: an <a> that gets the class "active" on the current page),
                          holding a KeywardIcon (svg.kw-icon) followed by a <span> with the text — a collapsed
                          icon-only sidebar can hide the span; the title attribute carries the text as a tooltip.
   Unstyled, the links still work and read as a plain list. *@
@inject IStringLocalizer<SharedResource> Loc

<AuthorizeView>
    <Authorized>
        <div class="nav-group-label">@Loc["Nav.Group.Vaults"]</div>
        <NavLink class="nav-link" href="@KeywardRoutes.Vaults" title="@Loc["Nav.Vaults"]"><KeywardIcon Name="lock" /><span>@Loc["Nav.Vaults"]</span></NavLink>
        <NavLink class="nav-link" href="@KeywardRoutes.AgentTokens" title="@Loc["Nav.AgentTokens"]"><KeywardIcon Name="key" /><span>@Loc["Nav.AgentTokens"]</span></NavLink>

        <div class="nav-group-label">@Loc["Nav.Group.Software"]</div>
        @* Applications now hold their own data (secrets) and client tokens as tabs — one nav entry. *@
        <NavLink class="nav-link" href="@KeywardRoutes.Applications" title="@Loc["Nav.Applications"]"><KeywardIcon Name="package" /><span>@Loc["Nav.Applications"]</span></NavLink>
    </Authorized>
</AuthorizeView>
